# Rust / Cargo
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed — this workspace ships binaries (chapr-coord,
# chapr-endpoint), so the lockfile is tracked for reproducible builds
# (Rust guidance for applications).

# Coordinator runtime artifacts (in case coord is run with default paths in-repo).
chapr-blobs/
*.db
*.db-*

# MCPB bundle staging + packed deliverable. build-mcpb.ps1 defaults to
# -OutDir ./build and copies target/release/chapr-endpoint.exe into it.
build/
*.mcpb

# Scratch working dir.
scratchpad/

# Local editor/OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.log

# --- Internal development tooling — kept LOCAL, never published. -------------
# The code is the product; these are private working docs / agent tooling.
# (gitignore does not delete them — they remain on disk for local use.)
#
# `LOGBOOK.md` and `CLAUDE.md` used to be here. They are committed as of
# 2026-08-14: the logbook is ~110 KB of irreplaceable project memory — decisions,
# their reasoning, and every issue's history — and keeping it out of git left it on
# one laptop with no backup. The repo is private, so there was never a disclosure
# argument against it, only "the code is the product". The reasoning behind the
# code turns out to be part of the product.
.claude/
docs/init spec/
docs/status.html
